course: dictionary
lesson: 5368
title: Kitten and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Look at the words around the new word, because they are its context and often give clues. «A girl in Vancouver is given a new kitten.» You can be given a pet, and a new pet is an animal, so a kitten must be an animal, probably a small one.
explain: «Kneading ... starts with kittens feeding from their mother» tells you more. Feeding from a mother means drinking her milk, which only very young animals do. So kitten must mean a young cat. Always test your meaning: put «a young cat» in the sentence instead of kitten and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words carry feelings or are used in phrases. A kitten can also be a loving name for something small and cute. «To have kittens» is an informal phrase meaning to be very worried. You would not guess this from the single words, so when the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A kitten is a young cat.
fact: Kittens grow into adult cats.
fact: Kittens are mammals, and they drink their mother's milk.
fact: A group of kittens is called a litter.
fact: Kittens need food, warmth, play, a litter tray and visits to the vet.
exercise: «A girl in Vancouver is given a new kitten.» What is a kitten? | A small dog | A type of blanket | *A young cat | A kind of car
exercise: «Kittens and puppies spend even more time in this busy sleep than grown-up cats and dogs.» Find and copy the word that means young cats. | *kittens | sleep | grown-up | busy
exercise: Ella says, «I'm having kittens before my test!» What does she mean? | *She is very worried | She has lost her cat | She wants a pet kitten | She is very happy and purring
test: Which fact about kittens is true? | They grow into dogs | *They drink their mother's milk | They have no paws | They are fish that live in rivers
test: Which phrase means very weak? | *as weak as a kitten | a litter of kittens | have kittens | a litter tray
exam: In stories a kitten often stands for something small, playful or helpless. What might a kitten stand for in a story? | *Something small, playful or helpless | Something that can fly high in the sky | A type of weather | Something huge and fierce
